{"abstract": [{"text": "A pull-down button displays a menu of items or actions that directly relate to the button\u2019s purpose.", "type": "text"}], "hierarchy": {"paths": [["doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/technologies", "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/human-interface-guidelines", "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/components", "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/menus-and-actions"]]}, "identifier": {"interfaceLanguage": "swift", "url": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/pull-down-buttons"}, "kind": "article", "legalNotices": {"copyright": "Copyright &copy; 2026 Apple Inc. All rights reserved.", "privacyPolicy": "https://www.apple.com/privacy/privacy-policy", "termsOfUse": "https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/terms/site.html"}, "metadata": {"availableLanguages": ["en-US", "zh-CN", "ja-JP", "ko-KR"], "customMetadata": {"supported-platforms": "ios,ipados,macos,visionos"}, "images": [{"identifier": "components-pull-down-buttons-thumbnail.png", "type": "card"}], "role": "article", "title": "Pull-down buttons"}, "primaryContentSections": [{"content": [{"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "components-pull-down-button-intro.png", "type": "image"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"text": "After people choose an item in a pull-down button\u2019s menu, the menu closes, and the app performs the chosen action.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "Best-practices", "level": 2, "text": "Best practices", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Use a pull-down button to present commands or items that are directly related to the button\u2019s action.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " The menu lets you help people clarify the button\u2019s target or customize its behavior without requiring additional buttons in your interface. For example:", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"items": [{"content": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "An Add button could present a menu that lets people specify the item they want to add.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}]}, {"content": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "A Sort button could use a menu to let people select an attribute on which to sort.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}]}, {"content": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "A Back button could let people choose a specific location to revisit instead of opening the previous one.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}]}], "type": "unorderedList"}, {"inlineContent": [{"text": "If you need to provide a list of mutually exclusive choices that aren\u2019t commands, use a ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/pop-up-buttons", "isActive": true, "overridingTitle": "pop-up button", "overridingTitleInlineContent": [{"text": "pop-up button", "type": "text"}], "type": "reference"}, {"text": " instead.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Avoid putting all of a view\u2019s actions in one pull-down button.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " A view\u2019s primary actions need to be easily discoverable, so you don\u2019t want to hide them in a pull-down button that people have to open before they can do anything.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Balance menu length with ease of use.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " Because people have to interact with a pull-down button before they can view its menu, listing a minimum of three items can help the interaction feel worthwhile. If you need to list only one or two items, consider using alternative components to present them, such as buttons to perform actions and toggles or switches to present selections. In contrast, listing too many items in a pull-down button\u2019s menu can slow people down because it takes longer to find a specific item.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Display a succinct menu title only if it adds meaning.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " In general, a pull-down button\u2019s content \u2014 combined with descriptive menu items \u2014 provides all the context people need, making a menu title unnecessary.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Let people know when a pull-down button\u2019s menu item is destructive, and ask them to confirm their intent.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " Menus use red text to highlight actions that you identify as potentially destructive. When people choose a destructive action, the system displays an ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/action-sheets", "isActive": true, "overridingTitle": "action sheet", "overridingTitleInlineContent": [{"text": "action sheet", "type": "text"}], "type": "reference"}, {"text": " (iOS) or ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/popovers", "isActive": true, "overridingTitle": "popover", "overridingTitleInlineContent": [{"text": "popover", "type": "text"}], "type": "reference"}, {"text": " (iPadOS) in which they can confirm their choice or cancel the action. Because an action sheet appears in a different location from the menu and requires deliberate dismissal, it can help people avoid losing data by mistake.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Include an interface icon with a menu item when it provides value.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " If you need to clarify an item\u2019s meaning, you can display an ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/icons", "isActive": true, "overridingTitle": "icon", "overridingTitleInlineContent": [{"text": "icon", "type": "text"}], "type": "reference"}, {"text": " or image after its label. Using ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/sf-symbols", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": " for this purpose can help you provide a familiar experience while ensuring that the symbol remains aligned with the text at every scale.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "Platform-considerations", "level": 2, "text": "Platform considerations", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "No additional considerations for macOS or visionOS. Not supported in tvOS or watchOS.", "type": "text"}], "type": "emphasis"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "iOS-iPadOS", "level": 3, "text": "iOS, iPadOS", "type": "heading"}, {"content": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "You can also let people reveal a pull-down menu by performing a specific gesture on a button. For example, in iOS 14 and later, Safari responds to a touch and hold gesture on the Tabs button by displaying a menu of tab-related actions, like New Tab and Close All Tabs.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}], "name": "Note", "style": "note", "type": "aside"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Consider using a More pull-down button to present items that don\u2019t need prominent positions in the main interface.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " A More button can help you offer a range of items where space is constrained, but it can also hinder discoverability. Although people generally understand that a More button offers additional functionality related to the current context, the ellipsis icon doesn\u2019t necessarily help them predict its contents. To design an effective More button, weigh the convenience of its size against its impact on discoverability to find a balance that works in your app.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"columns": [{"alignment": "leading", "content": [{"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "menu-secondary-actions-collapsed.png", "metadata": {"deviceFrame": "iPhone16"}, "type": "image"}], "type": "paragraph"}], "size": 1}, {"alignment": "leading", "content": [{"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "menu-secondary-actions-expanded.png", "metadata": {"deviceFrame": "iPhone16"}, "type": "image"}], "type": "paragraph"}], "size": 1}], "numberOfColumns": 2, "type": "row"}, {"anchor": "Resources", "level": 2, "text": "Resources", "type": "heading"}, {"anchor": "Related", "level": 4, "text": "Related", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/pop-up-buttons", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/buttons", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/menus", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "Developer-documentation", "level": 4, "text": "Developer documentation", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/SwiftUI/MenuPickerStyle", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": " \u2014 SwiftUI", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/UIKit/UIControl/showsMenuAsPrimaryAction", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": " \u2014 UIKit", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppKit/NSPopUpButton/pullsDown", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": " \u2014 AppKit", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "Change-log", "level": 2, "text": "Change log", "type": "heading"}, {"header": "row", "rows": [[[{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Date", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}], [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Changes", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}]], [[{"inlineContent": [{"text": "September 14, 2022", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}], [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Refined guidance on designing a useful menu length.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}]]], "type": "table"}], "kind": "content"}], "schemaVersion": {"major": 0, "minor": 3, "patch": 0}, "sections": [], "topicSectionsStyle": "compactGrid", "references": {"components-action-sheets-thumbnail.png": {"alt": "A stylized representation of a set of action sheet buttons. The image is tinted red to subtly reflect the red in the original six-color Apple logo.", "identifier": "components-action-sheets-thumbnail.png", "type": "image", "variants": [{"traits": ["2x", "light"], "url": "/images/com.apple.HIG/components-action-sheets-thumbnail@2x.png"}, {"traits": ["2x", "dark"], "url": "/images/com.apple.HIG/components-action-sheets-thumbnail~dark@2x.png"}]}, "components-buttons-thumbnail.png": {"alt": "A stylized representation of a button. The image is tinted red to subtly reflect the red in the original six-color Apple logo.", "identifier": "components-buttons-thumbnail.png", "type": "image", "variants": [{"traits": ["2x", "light"], "url": "/images/com.apple.HIG/components-buttons-thumbnail@2x.png"}, {"traits": ["2x", "dark"], "url": "/images/com.apple.HIG/components-buttons-thumbnail~dark@2x.png"}]}, "components-menus-and-actions-thumbnail.png": {"alt": "A stylized representation of a selected menu item, suggesting menus and actions. The image is tinted red to subtly reflect the red in the original six-color Apple logo.", "identifier": "components-menus-and-actions-thumbnail.png", "type": "image", "variants": [{"traits": ["2x", "light"], "url": "/images/com.apple.HIG/components-menus-and-actions-thumbnail@2x.png"}, {"traits": ["2x", "dark"], "url": "/images/com.apple.HIG/components-menus-and-actions-thumbnail~dark@2x.png"}]}, "components-menus-thumbnail.png": {"alt": "A stylized representation of a menu containing a selected item and displaying a s